                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:53.870-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>Comfortable walking shoes&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>An appetite: skip breakfast&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>A bag for what you will want to take home&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:53.871-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}6"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-27T14:52:28.264-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;p>We meet at ten by the oldest covered market in Paris, and begin with coffee and a croissant still warm from the oven of a baker two streets away. From there the walk follows the guide's own shopping route: a cheese shop where we taste five cheeses from mild to strong, a stall in the old Jewish quarter for falafel, a charcuterie, and a chocolate maker who lets visitors into the workshop. Between stops there are courtyards and a seventeenth-century square to see. We end at about three around a table in a wine bar, with a glass and whatever we bought along the way.&lt;/p>"
